--- A part's function names a column by its own loop's variable
--- (`df.`k``) however the entry names its variables: with a `k` at the
--- entry's top level, the part's `k` is renamed apart (`k__lib_columns`)
--- and the name inside the backticks had been left as the entry's,
--- refused as "a module variable, which a function does not see" — read
--- and written, in both modes (found porting Magpie's executor).
use frame
use lib/columns

k = 7
f = frame.new[a = [1, 2], b = [3, 4]]
log[columns.total_of[f, ['a', 'b']]]
log[columns.doubled[f, ['a', 'b']].b]
log[k]
